    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "As a 21-year-old physics and chemistry student in Milan, I see math as the backbone of understanding the natural world. It’s practical and intuitive for me—like how equations describe motion or chemical reactions. I enjoy its logical structure but find it more engaging when connected to real-world applications.",
